{"repoName":"Effect-TS/effect","result":{"ok":true,"data":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"For Effect v4/platform, the `KeyValueStore` service provides basic operations for durable storage, which can be used for idempotency or model-attempt records in a serverless proxy. The available native operations include `get`, `set`, `remove`, `clear`, `size`, `modify`, `modifyUint8Array`, `has`, and `isEmpty` . While there isn't a direct atomic `put-if-absent` or `compare-and-set` operation exposed at the `KeyValueStore` interface level, the `modify` and `modifyUint8Array` methods offer a way to update values conditionally based on their current state . For structured observations, the `Logger` module provides `Effect.logInfo` and other logging methods th<truncated omitted_approx_tokens="2359" /> Splunk or ELK .\n    ```ts\n    import { Effect, Logger } from \"effect\"\n\n    const productionProgram = Effect.gen(function*() {\n      yield* Effect.log(\"Server started\", { port: 3000, env: \"production\" })\n      yield* Effect.logInfo(\"Request received\", {\n        method: \"GET\",\n        path: \"/api/users\"\n      })\n      yield* Effect.logError(\"Database error\", { error: \"Connection timeout\" })\n    }).pipe(\n      Effect.annotateLogs(\"service\", \"api-server\"),\n      Effect.withLogSpan(\"request-processing\"),\n      Effect.provide(Logger.layer([Logger.formatJson]))\n    )\n    ```\n    \n\nYou can provide these loggers using `Effect.provide(Logger.layer([Logger.formatStructured]))` or `Effect.provide(Logger.layer([Logger.formatJson]))`  . The `Effect.annotateLogs` and `Effect.withLogSpan` combinators can be used to add contextual information to your logs, which is crucial for tracing and debugging in serverless environments  .\n\n## Notes\n\nThe `BackingPersistence` interface  is a lower-level abstraction for key-value storage that supports `get`, `set`, `remove`, and `clear` with optional TTL . While it has similar operations to `KeyValueStore`, `KeyValueStore` is specifically designed for string or binary values and offers `modify` operations . The `PersistenceStore` interface  is another related abstraction that stores `Exit` results for `Persistable` requests, which is used in higher-level persistence APIs like `PersistedQueue` for idempotency . The user's query specifically mentioned `KeyValueStore`, so the answer focused on that API.\n\nWiki pages you might want to explore:\n- [Cause and Error Handling (Effect-TS/effect)](/wiki/Effect-TS/effect#2.4)\n- [Durable Primitives and Persistence (Effect-TS/effect)](/wiki/Effect-TS/effect#6.4)\n\nView this search on DeepWiki: https://deepwiki.com/search/for-effect-v4platform-what-nat_965bd082-f355-4b89-81a8-b57cfe27864f\n"},"isError":false}}}
